    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d695">

                <pb facs="0627" n="618" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg618"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 M 956/282</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Mr. Robert D. Murphy </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-11-15">November 15,
                        1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s instruction
                    of this date<anchor n="91" xml:id="d695-f1"/> by which you were directed to
                    return to your post at Vichy, you are now instructed, after your return to your
                    post, to proceed to North Africa and to such other areas as may be necessary to
                    carry out instructions which have been given you verbally.</p>
                <p>[Here follows transportation authorization, etc.]</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Breckinridge Long</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
